---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import ArchitectureDiagram from '../../components/ArchitectureDiagram.astro';
import { url } from '../../utils/paths';

const pageTitle = "System Architecture & Engineering Specification";
const pageDesc = "In-depth architecture reference of AutoTelegramForward: Python Core, Go API Gateway, gRPC transport, durable queues, and fail-closed tenant isolation.";
---

<DocsLayout
  title={pageTitle}
  description={pageDesc}
  breadcrumbs={[
    { name: 'Architecture', href: url('/architecture/') }
  ]}
  prev={{ title: 'Verification', href: url('/getting-started/verification/') }}
  next={{ title: 'Operations & Troubleshooting', href: url('/operations/') }}
>
  <div class="space-y-8">
    <p class="text-base text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
      AutoTelegramForward is engineered as a decoupled, asynchronous microservices platform designed for high availability, zero message loss, and strict multi-tenant isolation.
    </p>

    <!-- Visual Architecture Component -->
    <div class="not-prose my-6">
      <ArchitectureDiagram />
    </div>

    <h2 id="service-breakdown">Microservice Responsibilities</h2>

    <div class="space-y-4 not-prose my-6 text-xs">
      
      <!-- atf-core -->
      <div class="p-5 rounded-xl bg-slate-900 border border-sky-500/30">
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-2">
          <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-white font-mono">1. Python Core (atf-core) — Port 50051</h3>
          <span class="px-2 py-0.5 rounded text-[11px] font-mono bg-sky-950 text-sky-400 border border-sky-800">gRPC Server & MTProto Engine</span>
        </div>
        <p class="text-slate-300 mb-3 leading-relaxed font-sans">
          The central data plane for AutoTelegramForward. Implemented in Python 3.12 with Pyrogram, <code>asyncio</code>, and SQLAlchemy.
        </p>
        <ul class="space-y-1.5 text-slate-400 font-sans list-disc ml-4">
          <li><strong>ClientPool:</strong> Manages persistent MTProto TCP sessions to Telegram Data Centers (DC2/DC4) for both bot tokens and user accounts. Handles reconnects and FloodWait auto-pause.</li>
          <li><strong>Pipeline Engine:</strong> Deterministic 5-stage sequential processing (<code>NORMALIZE</code> → <code>ROUTE</code> → <code>FILTER</code> → <code>CLEAN</code> → <code>TRANSFORM</code>).</li>
          <li><strong>DurableQueue:</strong> SQLite/PostgreSQL-backed lease queue worker pool. Retries transient delivery errors with jittered exponential backoff.</li>
          <li><strong>Album Aggregator:</strong> Groups multipart media updates using an 800ms debounce timer before dispatching unified <code>send_media_group</code> requests.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <!-- atf-api -->
      <div class="p-5 rounded-xl bg-slate-900 border border-slate-800">
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-2">
          <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-white font-mono">2. Go API Gateway (atf-api) — Port 8080</h3>
          <span class="px-2 py-0.5 rounded text-[11px] font-mono bg-emerald-950 text-emerald-400 border border-emerald-800">High-Concurrency REST API</span>
        </div>
        <p class="text-slate-300 mb-3 leading-relaxed font-sans">
          Built in Golang for maximum concurrency and minimal memory overhead. Acts as the public ingress for HTTP clients and the Web Dashboard.
        </p>
        <ul class="space-y-1.5 text-slate-400 font-sans list-disc ml-4">
          <li>Translates incoming REST requests into gRPC calls routed to <code>atf-core:50051</code>.</li>
          <li>Enforces JWT authentication and verifies tenant ownership before dispatching gRPC RPCs.</li>
          <li>Serves system health probes at <code>/health</code> with sub-millisecond response latency.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <!-- atf-logger -->
      <div class="p-5 rounded-xl bg-slate-900 border border-slate-800">
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-2">
          <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-white font-mono">3. Logger Service (atf-logger) — Port 50052</h3>
          <span class="px-2 py-0.5 rounded text-[11px] font-mono bg-purple-950 text-purple-400 border border-purple-800">Structured Telemetry</span>
        </div>
        <p class="text-slate-300 mb-3 leading-relaxed font-sans">
          Dedicated gRPC service capturing structured pipeline telemetry events (<code>[PIPELINE:...]</code>) and audit events, preventing disk I/O bottlenecks in the core forwarding path.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- atf-web -->
      <div class="p-5 rounded-xl bg-slate-900 border border-slate-800">
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-2">
          <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-white font-mono">4. Web Dashboard (atf-web) — Port 8088</h3>
          <span class="px-2 py-0.5 rounded text-[11px] font-mono bg-amber-950 text-amber-400 border border-amber-800">React Frontend</span>
        </div>
        <p class="text-slate-300 mb-3 leading-relaxed font-sans">
          Responsive web UI built with React, Vite, and Tailwind CSS. Allows visual management of forwarding tasks, real-time message stream inspection, and rule configuration.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>

    <h2 id="pipeline-lifecycle">Message Forwarding Pipeline Lifecycle</h2>
    <p>
      Every incoming Telegram event follows a strict, non-blocking lifecycle:
    </p>

    <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-slate-950 border border-slate-800 font-mono text-xs my-4 space-y-2 text-slate-300">
      <div><span class="text-sky-400 font-bold">1. [MTPROTO:INGEST]</span> Message arrives via Pyrogram event handler.</div>
      <div><span class="text-sky-400 font-bold">2. [PIPELINE:NORMALIZE]</span> Normalizes UTF-16 surrogates to Python str; buffers albums if media_group_id is present.</div>
      <div><span class="text-sky-400 font-bold">3. [PIPELINE:ROUTE]</span> Queries ForwardRules matching <code>(source_chat_id, user_id)</code>. Dropped if inactive or suspended.</div>
      <div><span class="text-sky-400 font-bold">4. [PIPELINE:FILTER]</span> Evaluates Media Type blocks, Link filter, Whitelist, and Blacklist. If rejected, emits <code>[PIPELINE:FILTER_DROP]</code>.</div>
      <div><span class="text-sky-400 font-bold">5. [PIPELINE:CLEAN]</span> Strips URLs, @mentions, #hashtags, emojis, phones, or custom words.</div>
      <div><span class="text-sky-400 font-bold">6. [PIPELINE:TRANSFORM]</span> Interpolates Header/Footer shortcodes and applies Regex replacements.</div>
      <div><span class="text-sky-400 font-bold">7. [PIPELINE:QUEUE]</span> Enqueues delivery payload into DurableQueue with lease lock.</div>
      <div><span class="text-sky-400 font-bold">8. [PIPELINE:DELIVERED]</span> Dispatches to destination chat via MTProto. Logs completion.</div>
    </div>

    <h2 id="durability">Durable Queue & Lease-Based Workers</h2>
    <p>
      To prevent message loss during service restarts or network partitions, forwarding jobs are persisted in SQLite/PostgreSQL with lease semantics:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Worker Leases:</strong> When a worker takes a job, it acquires a 60-second lease lock.</li>
      <li><strong>Automatic Failover:</strong> If a worker crashes mid-delivery, the lease expires and another worker immediately reclaims the task.</li>
      <li><strong>Idempotency:</strong> <code>MessageMap</code> records the mapping between <code>(source_chat_id, source_message_id)</code> and <code>(dest_chat_id, dest_message_id)</code> to prevent duplicate deliveries.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</DocsLayout>
